    {
      "id": 13,
      "code": "G",
      "title": "Prepositions of time (at / on / in)",
      "rule": "Vaqt predloglari uchta: *at* — soat va baʼzi soʻzlar bilan: *at seven, at night, at the weekend*. *On* — hafta kunlari bilan: *on Monday, on Sunday*. *In* — oylar, fasllar va kun qismlari bilan: *in May, in summer, in the morning, in the evening*. *I get up at seven.* — Men soat yettida turaman. *We go to the park on Sunday.* — Biz yakshanba kuni parkka boramiz. *It is cold in winter.* — Qishda sovuq boʻladi.",
      "examples": [
        "I get up at seven.",
        "We have lunch at one.",
        "Bekzod plays football on Saturday.",
        "Dilnoza works in the morning.",
        "It is cold in winter.",
        "My birthday is in May."
      ],
      "words": [
        { "en": "at seven", "uz": "soat yettida" },
        { "en": "at night", "uz": "kechasi" },
        { "en": "at the weekend", "uz": "dam olish kunlari" },
        { "en": "on Monday", "uz": "dushanba kuni" },
        { "en": "in the morning", "uz": "ertalab" },
        { "en": "in summer", "uz": "yozda" },
        { "en": "winter", "uz": "qish" },
        { "en": "birthday", "uz": "tugʻilgan kun" }
      ],
      "text": {
        "title": "Bekzod's week",
        "en": "Bekzod gets up at seven. He goes to school at eight. He plays football on Monday and Wednesday. On Friday he helps his father on the farm. At the weekend he visits his grandmother. In the evening he does his homework. He goes to bed at eleven. In summer he doesn't go to school. His birthday is in June."
      },
